      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q1",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:104mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q01-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Curve with intercept, turning point and asymptote.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span></p><p>The curve</p><ul><li>passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-1, 0)\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>has a maximum turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(2, 7)\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>has a horizontal asymptote with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3\"></span></li></ul><p>On separate diagrams, sketch the curve with equation</p><p>(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x + 2)\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = -f(x)\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>On each diagram, show clearly the coordinates of the points to which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are transformed and the equation of the asymptote.</p>",
