    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> passes through the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-3, 0)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, 22\\right)\"></span></p><p>(a) Find the equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = mx + c\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:102mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q02-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Region between the line and parabola.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> and the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, which intersect at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 2x^2 + 5x - 3\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li></ul><p>(b) use inequalities to define <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
