      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q11",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working. Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:94mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4. Semicylindrical feeding trough.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a design for a feeding trough.</p><p>The trough is modelled as a hollow, semicircular cylinder of radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> cm and length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> cm.</p><p>The trough will be made from sheet metal of negligible thickness.</p><p>Given that the capacity of the trough will be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90000\\pi \\text{ cm}^3\"></span></p><p>(a) show that the total area, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A \\text{ cm}^2\"></span>, of sheet metal required to make the trough is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A = \\frac{180000\\pi}{r} + \\pi r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Use calculus to find the radius of the trough for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is a minimum.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(c) Show that the radius found in part (b) gives the minimum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that the sheet metal costs £30 per square metre</p><p>(d) calculate the minimum cost of sheet metal required to make one trough.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(e) State one assumption you have made in calculating your answer to part (d).</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
