      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q12",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:100mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q12-figure-1.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5. Curve C and its two turning points.\"></figure><p>Figure 5 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>The curve has a minimum turning point on the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis and a maximum turning point in quadrant 2.</p><p>(a) On **Diagram 1**, sketch the graph of the gradient function for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>[A copy of Figure 5 has been included on the next page to help you.]</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The gradient function for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has **one** of the following equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx} = (x + 1)^2 - 2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 + 9x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx} = -x(x + 7)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx} = x^2 - 5x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(b) State the correct equation for the gradient function, fully justifying your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:104mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q12-figure-2.svg\" alt=\"Copy of Figure 5 and Diagram 1. Axes for the gradient function.\"></figure>",
