      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q13",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working. Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>The growth of a particular tree is monitored over a period of time.</p><p>The height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span> metres, of this tree, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years after it was planted, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h = 31 - Ae^{-kt}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> are positive constants.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>exactly 10 years after it was planted, the height of the tree was 6 m</li></ul><ul><li>exactly 20 years after it was planted, the height of the tree was 11 m</li></ul><p>(a) find a complete equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, giving the value of each of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>Use the equation of the model to answer parts (b), (c) and (d).</p><p>According to the model, there is a limit to the height to which this tree can grow.</p><p>(b) Deduce this limit.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(c) (i) Find the initial height of the tree.</p><p>(ii) Hence explain whether this is a suitable model for the early growth of the tree.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(d) (i) Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}\"></span>, giving your answer in simplest form.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(ii) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> for which the height of the tree is increasing at a rate of 30 cm per year.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
        "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q13-ms-p35-1.svg\" alt=\"Official mark scheme for original question 13; source page 35, segment 1 of 2. Includes the original working, marks, alternative methods and examiner guidance in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
