      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2025-june/q14",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show detailed reasoning.</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x) = (1 + kx)^8\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that the first 3 terms, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, of the binomial series expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span> are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1 + 8kx + px^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a constant,</p><p>(a) find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"g(x) = \\left(a - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)f(x) \\quad x \\neq 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that the first 3 terms, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, of the series expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)\"></span> are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac{2}{x} - 21 - 90x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(b) find the possible pairs of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
